gitx.go-56-\t// Hooks and fsmonitor are off for every command: RepoDir is shared with\ninternal/gitx/gitx.go-57-\t// executor worktrees and must not get to run code with our credentials.\ninternal/gitx/gitx.go-58-\targs = append([]string{\"-c\", \"core.hooksPath=/dev/null\", \"-c\", \"core.fsmonitor=false\"}, args...)\ninternal/gitx/gitx.go-59-\tcmd := exec.CommandContext(ctx, g.bin, args...)\ninternal/gitx/gitx.go-60-\tcmd.Dir = dir\ninternal/gitx/gitx.go-61-\t// Inherit nothing git-specific (GIT_DIR, GIT_INDEX_FILE, GIT_CONFIG_PARAMETERS ...).\ninternal/gitx/gitx.go-62-\tvar base []string\ninternal/gitx/gitx.go-63-\tfor _, kv := range os.Environ() {\ninternal/gitx/gitx.go-64-\t\tif !strings.HasPrefix(kv, \"GIT_\") {\ninternal/gitx/gitx.go-65-\t\t\tbase = append(base, kv)\ninternal/gitx/gitx.go-66-\t\t}\ninternal/gitx/gitx.go-67-\t}\n3:## Implementation\n4-\n5-### Steps\n6-1. New `internal/gitx/version.go`: add `var MinVersion = Version{2, 47, 0}`, `type Version struct{ Major, Minor, Patch int }` with `String()` and `Less(Version) bool`, and `func ParseVersion(s string) (Version, error)`. It parses the output of `git --version`, e.g. `git version 2.50.1 (Apple Git-155)` or `git version 2.39.5`. It takes the first three dot-separated numeric fields and tolerates a missing patch and vendor suffixes. Reason: one place owns the minimum.\n7-2. Same file: `func (g *Git) Version(ctx context.Context) (Version, error)`. It runs `git --version` through the existing unexported `run` (`internal/gitx/gitx.go:55`) with an empty dir, then calls `ParseVersion`. Also `func (g *Git) CheckVersion(ctx context.Context) error`. It returns nil when the version is >= `MinVersion`. Otherwise it returns an error like `git 2.39.5 is too old: ard needs git 2.47.0 or newer (the committer's fetches fail on older versions)`. It wraps a failure to run or parse git with a clear message.\n8-3. `internal/servecmd/serve.go`: right after `resolveRepo` succeeds (about line 72) and before `state.CheckLegacy` and `AcquireLeader`, call `gitx.New(\"\").CheckVersion(ctx)`. On error return `&cli.ExitError{Code: 1, Err: fmt.Errorf(\"ard serve: %w\", err)}`, matching the neighbouring checks. Reason: fail before any state, lock or clone work.\n9-4. `internal/configcmd/config.go` `Check`: call the same check first, before `config.RepoRoot`, and return `fmt.Errorf(\"ard config check: %w\", err)`. Do it unconditionally, so the check is the same with or without `--ref`.\n10-5. Docs: add one sentence to the local-executor/clone paragraph in `docs/proposal.md` (the line starting \"Local-executor details\") saying that `ard serve` and `ard config check` refuse to run on git older than 2.47.0. Keep the edit to one sentence. Add a short \"Requirements\" note to `README.md` only if it already has a setup section. Otherwise skip it.\n11-6. Leave the optional \"make the fetch work on 2.39\" part as a separate follow-up issue.\n12-\n13-### Test plan\n14-Command: `go test ./internal/gitx/... ./internal/servecmd/... ./internal/configcmd/...`, then `go test ./...`.\n15-- `internal/gitx/version_test.go`, table test `TestParseVersion`:\n16-  - `git version 2.39.5` -> {2,39,5}.\n17-  - `git version 2.50.1 (Apple Git-155)` -> {2,50,1}.\n18-  - `git version 2.47` -> {2,47,0}.\n19-  - `git version 2.48.0.rc1` -> {2,48,0}.\n20-  - `git version 2.51.0.windows.1` -> {2,51,0}.\n21-  - Failures: empty string, `garbage`, `git version x.y`.\n22-- `TestVersionLess`: compare across major, minor and patch boundaries, and equal versions.\n23-- `TestCheckVersion`: write a shim shell script into `t.TempDir()` that echoes a chosen version. The script should use `exec.LookPath(\"sh\")` or a `#!/bin/sh` line, as `internal/roles/cve_test.go` does. Build the Git with `gitx.New(shim)`. 2.39.5 gives an error containing both `2.39.5` and `2.47.0`. 2.47.0 and 2.56.1 give nil. A shim that prints junk gives a parse error. A missing binary gives an error.\n24-- `internal/servecmd/serve_test.go` (follow the existing harness): the old-git case is hard to inject because the call uses `gitx.New(\"\")`. To make it testable, pass the binary through a package var such as `var gitBin = \"\"` (new, in servecmd). The test sets it to a shim reporting 2.39.5 and asserts the `ard serve:` error, exit code 1, and that no state directory was created. Do the same for configcmd with `TestCheckRefusesOldGit`.\n25-- Edge: a patch-level difference below the minimum (2.46.9) is rejected.\n26-- Edge: existing tests must pass on the dev machine's git (2.50 or newer).\n27-\n28-### Risk\n29-Low. The change is additive and fails early. Risks:\n30-- The minimum is a conservative guess. Only 2.47.3 (pass) and 2.39.5 (fail) were observed, and no git between them is available here to bisect. A too-high minimum blocks operators needlessly. A maintainer should confirm, or run `go test ./internal/committer ./internal/gitx` against intermediate gits and lower `MinVersion`.\n31-- Hosts with a vendor git string (Apple, Windows) rely on the tolerant parser.\n32-- `ard config check` becomes dependent on git being runnable. It already uses git for `--ref`.\n33-- No protected paths in `merge.protected_paths` are touched. No migrations or concurrency. The public CLI behaviour changes only for old git.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Q9CA69B6wH62EB4jsdBZCJ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
